  "method": "Total variance is pair-sampling plus label noise. The pair-sampling standard deviation is recovered from the committed percentile bootstrap interval as its half-width divided by the normal quantile. Label noise is modelled as an independent flip with probability p per label, so the flip count on each class is binomial and its variance is n*p*(1-p); that count is carried into MCC by the per-flip sensitivity of the observed confusion matrix. The point estimate is held fixed, so this bounds the interval and is not a posterior.",
